#76002
"Within the Gypsy Camp"
"Wild colors run rampant here, like splashes of paint from an artist's palette
scattered over the ground.  Brilliant scarlets, lush greens, deep blues and
royal purples can be see everywhere you look, almost blinding in their
flamboyance.  A trail worn down by the passage of many feet threads its way
through the high grass, leading east and west.  A grove of willows lies just
to the north, while a large, elaborate wagon rests immediately to the south.
"
""
