#76032
"Fenced-in Pastureland"
"A silver-green swath of ankle-high grass whispers soothingly with every
dancing breeze, the verdant pasture stretching a good distance to the east and
north before meeting the rough-hewn fence.  Here and there, small patches of
lilies of the valley raise their heads skywards, drinking in whatever light
comes their way.  The air filled with the smells of earth, grass and horses,
not an unpleasant mixture.  The calls of several traders plying their wares
echo through the area.
"
""
