#76033
"Fenced-in Pastureland"
"Pale, silvery green grass stretches across the pasture, lush and thick as an
expensive carpet.  A wagon, smaller than many of those in this encampment,
stand just beyond the rough wooden fence to the west, its trappings a blaze of
chaotic color.  The enclosure extends to the east and south, bordered to the
north by the picketed fence.  The fresh smells of wind and rain mingle with
the odors of horses and hay, the comingling odd, but not entirely unpleasant.
"
""
