#76034
"Fenced-in Pastureland"
"The expanse of soft, pale green grass continues here, both inside this
enclosure and beyond the fence running to the east and north.  A clump of shy
violets take shelter in the slight shade provided by the rather shoddily
constructed fence, the lush purple hued petals a strong contrast to the
lighter tones of the grass.  Bright spots of burgundy are scattered throughout
the grassy area, undoubtedly clover blossoms.  Eastward, the southern trade
road can be glimpsed beyond the flower-dotted carpet of silvery green.
"
""
